#passage(("What do you mean by physical abuse? If we say, for instance, that somebody is committing a crime, whatever that crime is, and the police comes and they restrain him with power, physically, would we call that physical abuse? So on your worldview then, we don't do any type of harm or damage to any human being, no matter what they do? Then we'll all be slaughtered to death. That's it!", "Let's just apply this reality. You have a government today, in the Middle East, and you have Gaza, and you have all what's happening there, and you can see with your own eyes. You have a government indiscriminately unaliving people everywhere! All countries around them are being attacked. Now, in your worldview, you are not supposed to do anything to these people. And now, not only that, you have other governments who have powers, but they still continue to do what they're doing. You have people who try to restrain them, and they're still doing. Now, imagine if nobody is restraining them, imagine if there is nothing at all happening, except that this government is the one that does what they want. Do you think me and you would be alive?", "Allah says in the Quran (alBaqara2:216) كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْقِتَالُ وَهُوَ كُرْهٌۭ لَّكُمْ ۖ (Allah wrote upon you fighting, and you hate it). Who likes to go to war and lose their limbs, except for some maniacs? Nobody wants that! So Allah says that it's been written upon you. It's been obligated upon you to do, but you don't like it. And then Allah says: وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تَكْرَهُوا۟ شَيْـًۭٔا وَهُوَ خَيْرٌۭ لَّكُمْ ۖ (You may hate something, and it's good for you), (and you may like something, and it's bad for you, and Allah knows, and you do not know). It's very important. Allah says (alBaqara2:251) وَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلنَّاسَ بَعْضَهُم بِبَعْضٍۢ لَّفَسَدَتِ ٱلْأَرْضُ (If Allah did not use people to deter other people from evil, then the entire earth would be corrupted).", "So it's important that there are punishments that are applied. And these punishments, of course, use a level of \"violence\", or whatever term you want to use. It's necessary, because it's a deterrent! Not everybody lives in La La Land. Not everybody is \"Buddha\": \"oh, I'm going to become Buddha, and sit down and meditate\". Not everybody's going to do that! That's why every country has police officers, army, weaponry. Why are there no countries on earth that are applying that idea, \"oh, do whatever you want\"? Because they know! If we allow people to do whatever they want, there are multiple human-like animals who will just destroy the entire society and kill everybody and take everything. So it's necessary. It's just common sense that we may have certain types of punishments and deterrents that preserves people's rights and identities.", "Just because there is \"harm\", that doesn't mean it's wrong. This idea that \"harm\" equals \"wrong\" is something incorrect. There is good harm, there's bad harm. It's all based on justice: is it justifiable or not justifiable? If it's done for restraining, for preservation of life: someone is coming to do something to the entire population of a country, or has a weapon or whatever, and then you have to apply violence to that person. They will even use what they call \"deadly force\" to restrain that individual. We cannot just pick on the example; it's the idea itself. If someone goes and steals from the government, is he still punished? Yes! Will he be treated the same as if he stole a bank? Yes! He didn't harm any normal human being, it's paper being printed by the government, but the laws are still being applied! It's not just the concept of \"what kind of harm?\" There are laws that need to be applicable. The question is, who determines who needs to be punished and what is right and what is wrong? Where do you get that from? If you don't take it from God, you're going to take it from humans.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Lady Questions Muslim On Outdated Laws In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TGTUzypPFHI", ((204, "3:24–4:01"), (247, "4:07–4:47"), (297, "4:57–5:36"), (345, "5:45–6:31"), (400, "6:40–8:01"),))
