#passage(("Punishment for [adultery], the witnesses and all of that, is applied for both men and women. It's just a media thing. In fact, the Quran is clear about the punishments for fornication and adultery. It says, chapter 24 of the Quran, first few [verses], the exact reference says: let a group of the Believers (doesn't say men) witness the punishment.", "It's punishable by death; that's why I was telling you: adultery, not fornication. Fornication has a different ruling, because adultery is someone who's married, then he cheats, man or woman, and sleeps to someone else; and fornication, which is before marriage: someone commits the ACT. There's two separate punishments in Islam. So there's punishment by lashing, which is for fornication, not for adultery. So these are two separate punishments.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Couple Challenge The Islamic Paradigm! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bF9pKdBzqf0", ((1108, "18:28–18:54"), (1144, "19:04–19:32"),))
