// U ML049:244-276 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Islam has a punishment. And this verse in the Quran, by the way, in chapter:24 of the Quran, Surat anNur, in the first few verses, it mentions something important as well. It says (do not have any mercy for them) (anNur24:2), specifically those people who are being lashed. It's not just mentioning the punishment. And it also mentions a very specific thing that you see in this ruling: وَلْيَشْهَدْ عَذَابَهُمَا طَآئِفَةٌۭ مِّنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ (And let a group of the believers witness the punishment). Why is Allah saying in this specific punishment, which is a punishment of lashing, (have the believers witnessing it)? And you don't see this anywhere else in the Quran, by the way. You don't see the Quran saying in other punishments (and have a group of the believers witnessing it). Allah says, if you believe in Allah and the Last Day, apply this punishment, and have the believers seeing it, because it's a DETERRENT. The purpose behind the punishment is not the punishment itself; the purpose behind the punishment is to deter others from doing the same act. That's the main reason why we have this حُدود (Hudud: bounderies set by law) in Islam.", "That's why we have a rule: if you have any doubt, any شُبهَة (shubha), any doubt that a certain crime has been committed, then the punishment is NOT applied. Any type of doubt! So Islam, if you have the slightest doubt that someone has done this crime, whatever that type of doubt is, you don't have conclusive 100% evidence, then the punishment is not applied. So why? It's because, like I said, Islam is not trying to apply the punishments to the people.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Lady Questions Muslim On Outdated Laws In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TGTUzypPFHI", ((722, "12:02–13:05"), (788, "13:08–13:32"),))
