#passage(("I told him, you can see the harm effects of adultery in a community, in a society, because when adultery is done, in most cases it ends up by separation between the husband and the wife. And what ends up happening when separation happens between the husband and wife is that the woman becomes a single mother in most cases, because in the West, in most cases, they give the custody of the children to the mother. And 80 to 90% of the women anyways initiating the divorce, because they allow them to initiate the divorce here in the West. So they initiate the divorce, they take the child.", "And then I was mentioning to him a book by Warren [Farrell], it's called The Boy Crisis, where he just brings this amount of studies showing you that majority of the [degenerates], criminals, rapist, Killers, murderers, robbers in society come from single parent homes, specifically single mother homes, fatherless homes. Because when they look at single parent as a father, they see that it [fares] very close to both parents. But when it's a female that is leading the family, in that [case] there's not as much discipline there, not as much control. You can just speak to the child, but when the child becomes a teenager, now he's like a big body; he's not going to listen to anything, he's going to go do whatever he wants to do. Cannot discipline anymore. Cannot take the slippers like when he was young; the slippers [cannot] work anymore. You need a bigger weapon. And what ends up happening is that they become the [degenerates] in society.", "So I said to him: one life or two lives in the case of adultery, probably one life in this case, person who committed the adultery, saves how many lives when there's a law like this? First, it deters the individual from doing this thing. And it's very difficult to punish the adultery, so it will work as a deterrent. When you hear the punishment, it acts as a [deterrent]. So it's not like that this punishment will be applied, but people will know to be very careful not to do it. So it will stop this idea of adultery, and in the same time the [person] is not going to die, because he's going to deter from it, and it's very difficult to punish him. So I explain to him how many lives are saved from these people that will become the [degenerates] in society and will end up killing, raping, stealing, murdering; how many money is saved, how many people's rights are saved, how many lives are saved.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((2296, "38:16–38:50"), (2330, "38:50–39:51"), (2391, "39:51–41:02"),))
// U ML421:469-497 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("The reasoning is ALLAH SAID IT IS bad. But it's a wisdom we can see from our human perspective; this is some of the wisdoms we can see. Like I can tell you something without telling you the wisdom. But you look at it, you realise: \"Oh, actually, this guy is very wise. This is the wisdom behind why he was telling me not to do that.\" So we can see some wisdom. There's probably much more. It can destroy a woman's life. She can commit suicide. It's because she loves someone so much, and he cheated on her, and that happens. People commit suicide. Sometimes, they kill their partner because they know that he cheated on them. So you might not see the gravity of the crime, but if you look at the statistics, and what it causes in society, you'd realise there's so much wisdom behind that rule.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslims Question Islam P2! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AXViHAPPte0", ((1257, "20:57–21:41"),))
