#passage(("If you commit fornication or adultery, then the punishment is not instantly applied to you. How do we know that you did it? There needs to be a due process (then, that would be in an Islamic state). You have to have witnesses. It's not just any four people. It's FOUR, they have to be MALE specifically. So, if four women are walking, it's not enough. Four, and they have to be PRACTISING Muslim MEN. In Islam, testimony is just not accepted from random people, if a person is not known to have a good and just character. And look how many bad people are there! Now you need four practicing Muslim men that are righteous people, just people. You need four of them.", "And they need to, not just witness; like if they see them together going up the elevator or something, no, that's not enough! They literally need to see the ACT itself. The scholars actually go in detail of describing private parts. They have to describe that to the judge. The person has to testify: \"I have seen X\" (and of course, I'm not going to describe the situation), but he has to literally describe the process to the judge.", "Now, if we have four witnesses, three of them testify and one doesn't, they will all be lashed. THEY will be lashed! Because you cannot go and accuse someone's honour. So what does that mean? That means that you have to be certain, you have to take that responsibility. Maybe someone will say, I don't want to take that responsibility; maybe one of the other witnesses is going to do something and I'm going to end up being lashed! So you need these four people. Now tell me, what is the possibility today of us seeing this happening, except if you're doing it in the middle of the street? By the way, Islam commands that you cannot spy on people. So those practicing Muslim men cannot spy on, like, look from the window or something. They cannot do this. I would say it's impossible. Unless you do it in the street, I wouldn't even say it's highly unlikely, I would say it's impossible.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Lady Questions Muslim On Outdated Laws In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TGTUzypPFHI", ((831, "13:51–14:50"), (893, "14:53–15:18"), (922, "15:22–16:11"),))
// U ML421:395-468 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Why practising? For example, they cannot look in the window and see someone committing adultery, because you cannot spy. Allah tells you not to spy. So, if you are a practising Muslim, you wouldn't spy. If you spied, your testimony is not accepted, because you are going against Islamic rulings. Male is Islamic judgment. That's what Islam says.", "Allah put that criteria because He doesn't want to punish. Allah says in the Quran (anNisa4:147) مَّا يَفْعَلُ اللَّهُ بِعَذَابِكُمْ (What would Allah do with your punishment?) He's The Creator. He doesn't need to punish you or anyone. But Allah put it in a society to deter people from doing that. Because you do not see the gravity of that crime. When you commit adultery, when you break a family, when children are going to the streets, not having a family structure, there's so much things you're not seeing in that image. You think of it as just a simple lust that someone did something. No! There's much more to it. It can destroy society from within. That's why it's a big crime. That's why there is a big flag that Islam puts, which is \"oh, it's stoning!\" But then, if you go into the details, you'll see that Islam is so tolerant to the extent that you can't even imagine.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslims Question Islam P2! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AXViHAPPte0", ((1132, "18:52–19:07"), (1201, "20:01–20:40"),))
