#passage(("If he's still public about his disbelief, and he's a disbeliever, and he'll continue like this in his life, yes, he will be punished, because now he's causing a danger, not only to himself. He's causing a danger to his family that he would live with, that he will talk to them about him leaving his religion. He's also causing a danger to society, in which he will be placing doubts in their heart, being a Career Apostate. Many of them talk about how bad Islam is, and talk to people who are ignorant, which will cause harm in society, to the family and to the people. So since he has that kind of harm on the society, there is a punishment that is there, that is set in place for that reason: to protect the most important thing, which is the afterlife of those people, that are more important than this subject and individual.", "In Islam, for instance, the Prophetﷺ made one treaty. It's called the Treaty of Hudaibiya, in which one of the conditions was if one of the people who accepted Islam with the Prophet apostated, that he sends them back to the disbelievers. So some scholars would use that to say that if someone wants to leave the Islamic country, of course he can leave. Before he says that he left Islam, he can leave the country, go to a non-Muslim country. Why are you staying in a country where its law is telling you, you will be punished if you break the law? Why are you staying in a Muslim country? Because you are trying to cause corruption in the Muslim country! That's why you reject the sincere responses, the Time of Repentance and all of that, and you're outspoken about it. You can just go travel, go somewhere else, go to a country of disbelievers like you, and live with them. Nobody will tell you anything. Because disbelievers will exist until the Day of Judgment. The Prophet told us about the signs of the Day of Judgment, and one of them will be fighting disbelievers. So they will remain until the Day of Judgment. You'll always have the option to leave, if you wanted to leave.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tyson Hockley Grills The Muslim Lantern With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XGBP8LOEhg8", ((1886, "31:26–32:18"), (1946, "32:26–33:35"),))
