#passage(("How do we know that someone apostated? They have to announce it. So the only way you can know someone apostated is that that person comes out there and tells you: \"I have committed apostasy.\" Now, what happens when it's reported to the authority that they have apostated? They bring that individual, and there's something called \"the Period of Repentance.\" They will answer their questions. They will ask them: why did you leave Islam? What were the issues? They will bring them a Scholar. That's how Islam process is! They will bring them to a person of knowledge who deals with them, who talks to them.", "This was the case of a Jewish person who accepted Islam and then left it. There were two of the Companions, I believe, Abu Musa alAsh'ari (or Abu Sa'id alKhudri, one of them) and Mu'adh. And he was talking to him for over 20 days, trying to basically answer his doubts: explain, why did you leave the religion? What's wrong? So, they were trying to apply this Period of Repentance. So that's what's going to happen: you'll talk to the person, you'll try to bring them back to the Faith, you'll try to answer their doubts and remove their misconceptions, because this is what happens: people lie to you, tell you things which are not true.", "Now, how long is this period? It's minimum 3 days, and there's no limit, according to the judge. So if the judge sees this is working, the person is actually learning, he's actually realising that he's being deceived, it's actually learning now the reality and the Truth, this period can take a long time.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Apostate Reveals Her True Colours After Getting Exposed! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NTgbl-R9v_0", ((1484, "24:44–25:20"), (1523, "25:23–25:47"), (1551, "25:51–26:07"),))
