#passage(("What if someone believes in his heart that another religion is true? I would say that is IMPOSSIBLE. I would say it is impossible for someone to know about Islam, learn about Islam and know why Islam is true, because they became a Muslim or they are a Muslim. If they are a Muslim and they know the Truth of Islam, it is impossible for them to sincerely believe in their heart that anything else is true. And I'm saying that based [on] me researching Christianity, researching Hinduism, researching Buddhism. If there was even a little bit of a chance or a possibility, I would have told you that there is a chance or a possibility. I'm happy for you to bring any examples of a religion that someone might think is true, and I will show you how obviously ridiculous it is, that it is impossible for someone sincerely to think this is from God; not sincerely, but rather following their desires. Allah says in the (Quran28:50) فَإِن لَّمْ يَسْتَجِيبُوا لَكَ (if they do not respond to you) فَاعْلَمْ أَنَّمَا يَتَّبِعُونَ أَهْوَاءَهُم (then verily know that they're following their desires). There's no other options! So it's either they will obey and listen to the Prophet, or know that they're following their desires. Once a person listens to Islam and actually studies Islam, he will not have a shadow of doubt in his heart that Islam is the Truth.", "I do not think after learning about Islam properly that is possible. That's why that period of repentance is there. This is what we do: the علماء, the Scholars, they say we remove the doubts, the شبهات, anything which appears to be true while it's not true. So you bring that individual, and he did not study Islam; maybe he's got misguided. He didn't learn about Islam, then he left Islam. And I get many examples of that. Many people message me, especially younger generation, because the younger generation in the West, they get a lot of doubts, and then their family are not educated, so they leave Islam. And then they speak with me. I've not had one encounter in which they spoke with me and they had a reasonable answer to the answers I gave. All of them agreed: OK, that makes sense; if this is true, then I'll come back to Islam.", "The punishment is not applied straight away. Islam does not try to punish people; it's not the purpose of Islam to punish human beings! That's not what Allah wants to do. If He wanted to do, why would He rely on us doing the punishment? He would punish them Himself. But these laws are for us to govern our societies.", "You cannot just leave Islam; there has to be a reason. No one just wakes up one day and it's like: I feel like leaving Islam today! There has to be some sort of a reason, that they come across something. We're rational beings in the end; we don't act unless we got reasons to act. So if someone left Islam, they got a reason. So the first question we would always ask, and that's why I ask every \"Ex-Muslim\" who comes: Why did you leave Islam? Give me now a rational reason which shows that Islam is not true! If they do, I would not be Muslim myself; I'll say to them: OK, I'll join you! I'll give you a chance to do one of 2 things: either give me evidence, something clear that is objective, that Islam is false, which then we say OK, that could be a reason; or give me one religion alternative which has evidences that is true, is from God, in which a person can go to and say: OK, I'll follow this.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Enquires About Heaven In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NyrpGRsef5I", ((510, "8:30–9:45"), (599, "9:59–10:41"), (651, "10:51–11:01"), (675, "11:15–11:58"),))
