#passage(("When you say \"The Quran says there is no compulsion in religion\": we do not take the Quran in vacuum. You might look at the Quran in vacuum and try to come to your own understanding. We don't do that. We believe that this verse is about acceptance of religion: there's no compulsion in the acceptance of religion. You cannot force someone to accept Islam; we have no issues with that.", "You can read the verse and make up your own understanding, make up your own conclusions. Let's say I'm like you: I read the Quran, and this is how I understand it. Why should we take your understanding over my understanding? Everyone can play this game!", "So, the point is very simple: we, as Muslims, do not take the Quran in a vacuum. We take the Quran in its historical context and with the explanation of the person who brought it to us, which is the Prophet Muhammedﷺ. We have a reason of Revelation. If you open the books of Tafsir, the books of Exegesis, which are 1200 years before you were born, they existed and were written. They mention that there is a reason for the revelation of this verse. And there is a person who came to the Prophetﷺ with two of his children; they were Christian, and then he said: \"Shall I force them to accept Islam?\" He accepted Islam and they were Christian children; then the Prophet told him not to force them to accept Islam.", "So, we believe this verse is about the acceptance of the religion. Once a person accepts Islam, there are now obligations of Islam that become bound for him. There are punishments that become applicable; they are mentioned in the Quran, many of them. For example, Qisas: if you kill someone, you're killed in retribution. That's punishment! You'll still be forced! That punishment will be applied to you now, because the minute you accepted Islam, the rules of Islam are now all applicable to you. There is no contradiction in understanding that verse to mean that it's about forcing someone to accept Islam. We don't force anyone to accept Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Dramatic Apostate Confronts Muslim On Islamic Law! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8G6UoAmYjYU", ((113, "1:53–2:16"), (163, "2:43–2:54"), (180, "3:00–3:37"), (220, "3:40–4:27"),))
