#passage(("There are people who try to liberalize their own faith; they tell you what you want to hear. I don't tell you what you want to hear; I tell you what the religion teaches, no matter how people think about it today. So now, there is a due process in Islam that takes place. You ask why, what are the wisdoms. We look at the wisdom; it's very simple. That punishment is only carried under an Islamic State. That's why any Muslim country today, I believe most of them, if not all of them, do not apply this law. They don't follow it fully, holistically; they follow in some aspects, and some aspects they don't. So that's why you have apostates all over the Muslim world today that nobody's doing anything to them. If someone apostates here, one of the people standing with me on the table says today I leave Islam, nobody can do anything to them. That's not a [Sharia] State. And as I said, the one who carries the punishment is the [Sharia] government, and it has to be in the [Sharia] State.", "Now, in that [Sharia] State there is a law that bounds the community, which is [Sharia] law. Now that person, the minute he leaves the religion of Islam, not only himself, he's going to break that [Sharia], because he no longer believes this is God's law, but he's going to entice others to do so. So let's say I live in a [Sharia] State. [Sharia] state says: do not commit fornication, do not commit adultery, do not do these specific things. Okay, I want to sleep with women; who are you to tell me? I don't believe in your religion. I want to drink alcohol; who are you telling me not to drink alcohol here? I want to do that. So they will create what we'll call Division and separation within Society. I want to deal with interest. Why interest not allowed? I think it's fine. So it would become a subjective thing, and then you have one person leaving, a second person enticing other people, that will eventually create a group that wants to rebel.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Confron