#passage(("Now those people who are taken as \"Milku al Yamin\", how are they dealt with in Islam? I want to say also that many scholars, a lot of scholars, believe you cannot have intercourse with \"Milku al Yamin\" if that woman is not a Jew or a Christian; that's a big opinion that is taken in a lot of the schools of thought.", "Because they're taken as captives of war, it is a punishment for them that they are captives of war, so there are certain duties and jobs that they need to do. So they will serve whoever that person that's taken them. It's not like slavery, Atlantic slavery, and beating slaves and all of that. There's no such thing.", "Also, this idea of \"Milku al Yamin\" is not inherited, not like slavery was inherited: if the father is a slave and has a son, the son is also slave. No, in Islam \"Milku al Yamin\" is not inherited to the next generation. It's just that person, because that next generation is not responsible; the person who's taken as a captive of war is the one who is \"Milku al Yamin\". If a child is newly born, that child is not inherited; he's not also a \"Milku al Yamin\" as his mother was \"Milku al Yamin\".", "Not only that, Islam commands explicitly to free \"Milku al Yamin\". Allah says this is a good deed to do. So Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Albalad90:11-13) وَمَاۤ أَدۡرَاكَ مَا ٱلۡعَقَبَةُ (what would make you know what the good way is?) فَكُّ رَقَبَةٍ (freeing \"Milku al Yamin\"). That's the good way, that's the righteous way; you get rewarded for it. Not only that, it's one of the ways to give زكاة (Zakat: mandatory alms-giving). Every Muslim has to pay Zakah. One of the things that you do in paying the Zakah is to free \"Milku al Yamin\". Not only that, when you commit a sin there's something called the Expiation of Sins (Kaffara). So if I make a sin and I want to expiate the sin, a way to expiate the sin is to let that \"Milku al Yamin\" go. So Allah has made all of these options to free them, which will in the end anyways result in no longer having any \"Milku al Yamin\".", "Not only that, unlike slavery, you cannot take a free person and make him a servant. In fact the prophetﷺ said to us, \"Allah is the enemy of 3 people,\" and one of them is a person who takes a free person and he sells him as a slave; that's completely prohibited in Islam. The only way that can happen is in war: people who were coming to fight you in war, they were coming to kill you. And one of the options that can be done is \"Milku al Yamin\". But it's a punishment for them that they have to serve you; it's a kind of a community service. Today they have the jail and community service. It's a form of service that you will do to that individual.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Islam Allow The Practice Of Slavery?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_cTwoneuyrU", ((422, "7:02–7:15"), (447, "7:27–8:00"), (506, "8:26–8:41"), (527, "8:47–9:20"), (567, "9:27–10:01"),))
