m himself and go free. Now, in exchange of money, he can go to a Muslim judge. And at the time of 'Umar ibn alKhattab, there was someone who did not want to do that, and Umar ibn alKhattab told him to do it. Allah says in the Quran, and he mentioned the verse: فَكَاتِبُوهُمْ إِنْ عَلِمْتُمْ فِيهِمْ خَيْرًا ۖ.", "So, if he wants to go free, he goes to a judge, Muslim judge. He gives money, and in exchange of that, he goes free. So, Allah says, if you know in that person goodness, that they are a good person, they're not going to go, if you let them go free, kill and rape and steal and do evil; if they're a good person, then let them go free. Allah says: وَآتُوهُمْ. So, you help them with money: وَآتُوهُم مِّن مَّالِ اللَّهِ الَّذِي آتَاكُمْ ۚ. So, you even HELP them to go free, if they want to ransom themselves and go free. So, it's not like these people got no choice, that this is the only place that they can be; they actually have the freedom and the choice to go free, if they want to go free. So, whatever this understanding that I just gave you, what Milku alYameen is, it has nothing to do with the definition or understanding that people have about slavery. So, that slavery does not exist in Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Masked Apostate Confronts Muslim On Slavery In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=csEWg7fSWZE", ((755, "12:35–13:18"), (806, "13:26–13:49"), (831, "13:51–14:15"), (857, "14:17–14:56"), (901, "15:01–16:04"),))
