em, send them to the enemy and then get money. 2/ Or you can exchange them with other prisoners: you can send them and get some from the Muslim prisoners that were taken. 3/ And you can let them go free, completely, like the prophetﷺ, what he did at the conquest of Mecca: when he took the captives of the conquest of Mecca, he let them go free. 4/ Or you can even kill them, because those people were coming to kill you to begin with, so there is no doubt that they were coming to take your life. And at that time there was no prisons; so you can say another option is to put them in prison, there was no prison to put them in. So these are the options, and the last one is \"Milku al Yamin\".", "Now the leader of the Muslims, he looks at the situation of the Muslims: what do we need the most? Maybe there's a lot of prisoners that are taken, so let's exchange prisoners; maybe you need money now, so let's ransom them for money. So he looks what is the best situation, and then he behaves based on that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Islam Allow The Practice Of Slavery?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_cTwoneuyrU", ((263, "4:23–4:31"), (288, "4:48–4:58"), (302, "5:02–5:47"), (353, "5:53–6:47"), (410, "6:50–6:58"),))
