x is enough to say that they are a sex slave. But then, using that logic, one's wife would be a sex slave, one's partner, one's girlfriend or whatever, regardless if it's haram or halal. Now, speaking on a general note, they would be a sex slave because they're simply available for sex. So the key point here is forced. A person has to be forced into such an environment where they can be freely abused sexually in order for that to be called sexual slavery. So it is only rational to conclude that sexual slavery does not exist in Islam, since that which is defined as sexual slavery is strictly prohibited and punished, as demonstrated in our earlier arguments, in Islamic law or Sharia.",), "Farid Responds, “[DEBUNKED] Islam vs Women - Apostate Prophet”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fu7m4EFyuJc", ((464, "7:44–8:12"), (498, "8:18–9:10"), (550, "9:10–9:30"), (570, "9:30–10:15"), (623, "10:23–11:13"),))
