#passage(("First, I would ask you where did you get these stats from? I like to make sure that the information is correct. Depending on how they are farming them: you can not assume everyone is doing the same thing. I've been to farms. I have a friend that has a farm in Wales; we've been to his farm. He doesn't abuse animals. So these stats will include him — that the food is coming from there — but he grows them naturally, he leaves it to eat from the grass, and this and that.", "The one who makes the claim should provide the evidence. If I make a claim, if I say to you the Quran is true, you say: why? I say: look it up! It's not a fair thing to do.", "The point I'm trying to make is this: it all comes back to the idea of subjective and objective morality. If you're coming from a subjective point of view, if you believe morality is subjective, you can't argue from my morality. You don't believe in it! So let's argue from my morality. Allah says in chapter:16 (Al-Nahl) of the Quran: (He created the animals for our food and sustenance). This is my morality. (So you can ride on them, you can use them). I don't believe they have an equal moral value, and I don't think you do as well!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Vegan Gets Emotional! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-6NWYbDw18k", ((5, "0:05–1:00"), (118, "1:58–2:06"), (150, "2:30–3:12"),))
