#passage(("I'll address that question, which is actually an important question, because there are some Muslims who are misunderstanding this point. There was a group of scholars, let's say 30 or 40 years from now, that issued a specific Fatwa. They said that you're able to eat the meat in the Western lands because these Western lands, based on that fatwa, they were saying they were Christian lands. So they assumed that they are slaughtering the meat like Christians are supposed to slaughter the meat, not electrocuting the meat, because electrocuting the meat becomes Haram even if a Muslim does it, let alone if a Christian does it. You saying Bismillah or not saying Bismillah is not going to change the fact it's Haram to eat. So electrocuted meat, there's consensus that this is Haram, because it's considered Mayta (carrion). And Allah mentions that explicitly in the Quran chapter 5 (Almaida5:3).", "What these scholars believed at that time: it was not as prevalent as today to use this electrocution and all of these different factories. So they assumed that these people are slaughtering the meat. So Muslims are allowed to eat meat that is slaughtered by the people of the Book. If a Christian or a Jew slaughters the meat, he uses a blade and actually slaughters the animal, not shoots the animal, not electrocutes the animal; all of that is not accepted. So if there is a Christian or a Jew that actually slaughters the animal and the animal dies, the Muslim is allowed to eat from that meat. The same chapter, chapter:5 that I told you, after mentioning these things in verse:2, it goes onwards to explain the things that we are allowed to eat from the people of the Scriptures. It says (Al-Ma'ida5:5) (the food of those who have been given the Scripture, it becomes permissible for you). So, if it's a slaughtered meat by a Jew or a Christian, it’s permissible for a Muslim to eat. So if you go today to Kosher restaurant as a Muslim, because they do slaughter their meat, they don't electrocute it, it’s permissible for you to eat that meat, but if the meat is electrocuted it's not permissible for you to eat.", "So they base that on this Fatwa, or this ruling that was given by these scholars years and years before. Today the situation is completely different: today they do not slaughter the meat, they electrocute the meat. That's number one. Number two, the people who are doing this are not Christians anymore. This is no longer a Christian country or even a Christian majority. According to the last census, the Christians are less than 50% in England and Wales. So no one can come and say that England is a Christian country or is a Christian-majority country; no longer this is the case. And you'll see the people growing are the Muslims and Agnostics and Atheists. Christians keep going down since 2010.", "So if it's an Atheist slaughtering, the meat is completely impermissible even if he slaughters it, not even just electrocuted. If it's a Christian or Jew, it has to be slaughtered and it has to be from a Christian or Jew. Now the situation is they are Atheists, so we cannot eat their meat, and they electrocute the meat. So for a fact, we cannot eat the meat that they're doing. Therefore we have to eat specifically from Halal-certified; even Halal-certified, there is specific Halal-certified which can be trustworthy, for example in the UK like HMC, because they do regular checks and they make sure that it's actually slaughtered and not electrocuted. So this would be the answer to that question: you cannot go to McDonald's and say Bismillah and start eating. These people who are saying these things, they're completely saying incorrect things.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7bA8bsNs20", ((687, "11:27–12:08"), (733, "12:13–13:10"), (795, "13:15–13:48"), (841, "14:01–14:41"),))
