#passage(("You know what happens when the animals are frightened? They release certain germs in their blood, etc., because they're frightened, they’re shocked. So these things today, medically, we know the effects on animals. So what happens today? They electrocute the animal. The animal is not slaughtered. In Islam, the animal is slaughtered. So first, it feels the lowest level of pain when it's dying. It's just few seconds for the animals to feel pain, while electrocution can take up to 30 minutes according to some studies. So it's horrible for the animal. Number one.", "Number two, when the animal is electrocuted, it's not slaughtered. The blood remains in the body. So any diseases that are released in the blood remains in the blood, in the meat that you eat. But when we slaughter the animal and we let all the blood go, anything in the blood will come out. So the meat you eat will be healthy and beneficial for you. So why would you want to eat something that is not good for you?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “University Student Challenges Muslim On Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0eOxOwACYXE", ((757, "12:37–13:08"), (789, "13:09–13:28"),))
