#passage(("It's a good question, because this is a big problem, I think, widespread today in the society: there are a lot of people who give this kind of Fatwas. They say go and eat from the People of the Book. \"Can I eat in McDonald's?\" \"Yeah, they are from People of the Book!\" And this is absolute nonsense for many reasons. There was a fatwa in the past in which, at that time, most of the people were Christians in that community, in that country, and these people were slaughtering actually in the Islamic way. So in the past, that fatwa had a time in which it was applied. But today why is it an issue? For 2 main reasons.", "The first main reason is that the people in this country are no longer Christians anyways; they’re majority Atheists. If you look at this country from 2001 to 2011, from 72% Christian to 52%. If you check from 2011 to today, it's even more people leaving Christianity. The majority of the people today are either secular or from other religions. So if the majority of the people are not Christians, you cannot say this is a Christian country.", "The second thing, which is even the biggest problem: even if everyone in this country were Christians, they do not slaughter the meat, they electrocute the meat. And electrocuting the meat is Haram by consensus of all Muslims; Allahﷻ mentions that in the Quran (Almaidah5:3). So even if they were Christians, they're not slaughtering in the way which the people of the Book would do. On the other hand, I'll say something important: the Kosher shops, you can eat there, because the koshers, they slaughter in the Halal Kosher way. And if you go to like Golders Green or some areas here in the UK, you would have Kosher stores in which you can eat, because they are slaughtering the meat properly. They're not electrocuting the animal and killing the animal in that way.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Revert Asks Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2x1ZhIz1Hrw", ((284, "4:44–5:12"), (319, "5:19–5:40"), (349, "5:49–6:25"),))
