#passage(("There are certain foods and things that Allahﷻ says do not eat, and we don't eat, obeying Allah. He says to us don't do it, we don't do it! Allah says, for example, about alcohol, there are some benefits in it (alBaqarah2:219), meaning you can buy and sell it and win money from buying it and selling it. But he said there are many harms; the harms outweigh the benefits.", "Allah said in the Quran (alAn'am6:141) (Do not excess. Allah does not love those who excess). And also Allah says (alisra17:27) (Those who excess are the brothers of Satan). Meaning it's Haram: it's not allowed for someone to excess in anything, eating or drinking or spending money, anything. Cannot go to excess. The Prophet told us you cannot harm anyone or yourself, which means if eating a lot of sugar is going to harm you, then it's Haram. It's impermissible for you to eat it. And many of the scholars mentioned this, like Sheikh Islam [Ibn] alQayyim, Ibn Taymiyyah; many of them talked about how it is equally Haram for someone to eat something excessively that will harm him, just like it is for someone who would smoke. So anything that you would eat excessively in a way that will harm you — you harm your body that is not yours, is given to you by God as a Trust — then it's also Haram and you actually get sin for it. So excessiveness in anything is prohibited in Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Lady Questions Muslim On Evidence Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nk4EM0u0VNs", ((1522, "25:22–25:35"), (1566, "26:06–27:06"),))
