#passage(("The most important thing is this: it's not \"trust the book\". We've already proved the book is from God. Once you already establish the book is from God, then every detail of it is not going to be questioned. That's irrational, because we already established the basis, foundation, that this is from God. God knows more than me. If he's telling me do X, I will do it. We go to human beings more [knowledgeable] than us and we don't even question. You go to the doctor: \"Okay, take this medicine.\" \"Oh, but why this specific?\" You don't do that. You just take it: okay, go buy it, start taking it, because we know that person is more knowledgeable in that field. So we submit to their knowledge. We submit to the knowledge of the most high because we know this is from the most high. So that is the answer to any moral question.", "But when you look at pork, I don't know how someone can eat pork. Even if I was not Muslim, I'm not going eat pork. The reason being is: where does it live? Where does he eat? It lives in the filthiest of places, it eats the filthiest of places. It's a bowl of [filth] essentially; that's what you're eating. Let's be honest: it lives in [filth], it eats filth, and it dies in [filth].", "But this is the thing: there are people who will say to you it's the best thing I have. Doesn't mean it's good. It makes you feel a certain way, a good way, a fuzzy way; does not mean it's good for you. So to say just because something tastes good, therefore it's good: there are very poisonous mushrooms that probably taste amazing.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “University Students Surprise Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FTEkpj70bQ0", ((318, "5:18–5:58"), (358, "5:58–6:26"), (390, "6:30–6:46"),))
