#passage(("Regarding the mortgage: if a person engages in mortgage or engages in interest and Riba out of ignorance, when he learns that that thing is wrong, whatever it was done in the past, he is allowed to keep. Allahﷻ says in (Quran2:275) “فَمَن جَآءَهُۥ مَوْعِظَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ فَٱنتَهَىٰ فَلَهُۥ مَا سَلَفَ وَأَمْرُهُۥٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ\" (Whatever happened before learning that this is the truth, you can keep that). But from now, you have to leave the Riba.", "So now, if you are in the middle of a contract, what you can do is you pay everything now, whatever is left, you pay all in full to get out of that. And then you can keep the house, because whatever happened in the past is left, but from now you try to pay everything. If you didn't know and you engage in interest, then whatever happened in the past Allahﷻ out of His Mercy, He allows you to keep that thing. But from now on, you stop, you don't engage in interest, you don't deal with Riba or interest in any way or shape.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Man Realises The Contradictions In Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CR6_RG9qdVM", ((571, "9:31–9:52"), (603, "10:03–10:25"),))
