#passage(("If you are going to become a Muslim because you believe that Islam is the truth, the minute you accept the religion of Islam, everything you did in your past of these sins is forgiven. The prophet told us that Islam completely removes everything that was before, just like repentance does. So if you become a Muslim, you don't have to worry about the years in the past. But then you stop having this interest bank account and you get a bank account which has no interest, just a normal current account or whatever, and in case they give you anything, you just get rid of that money, because that's not good money; that's money that is using people. Essentially this whole idea of interest is about being the worst type of human being possible. But you don't do it after you become Muslim. You change that into doing things which are beneficial.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Rational Thinker Asks A Muslim Thought-Provoking Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=myrg5IOTPBI", ((385, "6:25–7:49"),))
