#passage(("It's not drums, something called Duf دُفْ. It's different than drums. It's a different instrument, and that instrument is only allowed in holidays, in أعياد, in celebration like Eid. Eid Alfitr and Eid Aladha: on that time, women can play these things in celebrations. But generally musical instruments are prohibited based on Hadith of the Prophet.", "Why do I need to? I listen to the Quran. It's a recitation. People who live their lives surrounded with certain actions, they take these things as necessities, because they've been used to them. They've been all their life using these things or doing these things. When I say to someone, for example, I never drink alcohol in my life, I never gamble in my life, some people do not understand that. That does not make sense to them, because in their communities they were born, every weekend they go to drink with their friends, in a dinner usually you get wine. So to them, it does not make any sense that never in your life have you drunk or never in your life have you smoked or done any drugs. I don't need to introduce music into my life because of that. What does music benefit you? So if I have an alternative which is the Quran, which does not only make you feel nice but it's a spiritual thing that gets you rewarded in the Afterlife, why do I need to use music for that? Allah said so. Is that not enough?", "Duf: but that's only, as I said, under certain circumstance -celebration- and by women. It's the exception, as we say. Exceptions don't make the rule! It's a very minute exception that we have. But all of the musical instrument Prophet explicitly prohibited them.", "A lot of people are addicted to music. Some people cannot go one day without listening to music; it's an addiction. It's harmful. Actually, the waves that you get from this music controls your behavior, has a lot of influence on your psychology. So Rock Music and Classical Music do not have the same effects on your body or your psychology when you're listening to them. There are studies on these ideas: on how they affect your body, etc. So it's simple for Muslims: the Quran is more than enough. You don't need to understand it, but it makes you feel some way. It's calming, gives you tranquility, peace, and it's soothing, and you do feel it has a spiritual aspect, even if you're not a believer.", "Musical instruments are impermissible. All of the music of today, degrading women, cursing, killing, and all of this nonsense: that's what music is. So that's what people listen to, and it has an effect on their behavior. It actually makes people -certain people- commit crimes, because when you hear something too much, there is a level of brainwashing that takes place; that's the tactic for media. As I said, the instruments themselves they have an effect on you.", "But when you ask me why is it impermissible? I said to you Allah said so. So the reasons I'm giving you, I don't want you to conflate it, to think that I'm giving you now reasons for why it's Haram, because I'm not. All I'm doing is I'm saying there could be some wisdom that we can see. Because Allah is The All-Knowing, is The All-Wise, and I'm not all-knowing and all-wise, it would make perfect sense that I do not know the details for why everything is right or wrong. So there are things that Allah tells us why it's Haram, He tells us why we should not engage in it. And there are certain things that you might think that this could be the reason or this could be the reason, if Allah doesn't tell you Himself.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Visitor Questions Muslim On Hadith! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aVaXUL-Us6s", ((322, "5:22–5:45"), (356, "5:56–7:36"), (470, "7:50–8:14"), (535, "8:55–9:39"), (593, "9:53–10:31"), (634, "10:34–11:04"),))
// U ML284:806-936 | The Muslim Lantern | 6
#passage(("And then you have the last thing I want to talk about: the Music. \"Is music Haram? No, there's a disagreement. My uncle, he said..\" Prophetﷺ said.. \"No! My uncle, My nephew..\" The Hadith is clear, the Sahaba said.. \"No no, the scholar who lives somewhere in the world, sometime in the world, hundreds of years ago, he said it is OK\"! So, why are people struggling with Music? People are struggling with Music because the Quran is not in their heart; Islam is not in their heart.", "Sheikh al-Islam Ibn alQayyim, what did he say? He said in his Nuniyah -he has a very beautiful piece of poetry- It starts with: نزِّهْ سماعَكَ إنْ أردْتَ سماعَ ذيـّـاكَ الغناءِ عنْ هذهِ الألحانِ. You can read these few poetry pieces; they influenced me a lot when I heard them. And then he said in the end a very beautiful statement, he said: حبُّ الكتابِ (Loving of the Book of Allah), وحبُّ ألحانِ الغِنا (And to love the music), في قلبِ عبدٍ (In a heart of a servant), لَيسا يجتمِعان (They can not gather together in one heart). There's NOT enough space for you to love the Quran, to know the Quran -the Book of Allah- and to know music at the same time.", "Those people who listen to music: tell them \"OK, tell me about this album?\" They will tell you the name of the Artist, when she died, when she lived. What is her album, \"this album is unreleased, but I listened to this album. I know this music here, that no one else heard\"! You ask them: Do you know Quran? \"I know alFatiha, Alhamdulillah. I start with alFatihah in the prayer.\" Anything else? \"Yes, قُلْ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدٌ (alikhlas112:1), man, what you are talking about! I'm memorising the Quran.\" Do you memorise anything else? \"No! It's good, enough! You know what you're reciting for your prayer.\" Do you know Tafseer (Exegesis) of the Quran? Have you read the Tafseer before? \"No.\" Do you know the description of the verses? Do you know the life of the Prophetﷺ? \"No.\" Do you know the Names of the Surahs (Chapters) even? \"No.\" How many Surahs in the Quran? Some people they don't know! If you ask some people today, the smallest chapter in the Quran? They don't know! The biggest verse in the Quran? Which are very basic things! Many people they don't know. But they would know the album that is unreleased! And the name, which year it was released, why it was unreleased! And they will tell you the whole story. But the verses of Allah, no! It's not there. And they will try to argue their BEST to criticise any Hadith which speaks about that, any statement that speaks about that.", "You find the Quran is CLEAR, it can not be clearer. وَٱسْتَفْزِزْ مَنِ ٱسْتَطَعْتَ مِنْهُم بِصَوْتِكَ (lure them with your voice) (alisrae17:63), and then all of the Salaf (Predecessors) saying: It's Music: غِناء, غِناء, غِناء. Clearly! وَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَشْتَرِى لَهْوَ ٱلْحَدِيثِ (And from the people who does لَهْوَ ٱلْحَدِيثِ). What is لَهْوَ ٱلْحَدِيثِ? That's why the music instruments are called أدوات اللَّهو (Amusement Tools). So أدوات اللَّهو is what? Is musical instrument, same word there: لهو. So these أدوات اللَّهو that the people use, Allah is saying that \"from the people who\" use these things is to misguide the people from the path of Allah. This is not my understanding! 'Abdullah Ibn Mass'ood, Moujahed, 'Abdullah Ibn 'Abbas.. Who do you want? Attaa'.. They learned from the Prophetﷺ. The تُرجمان (Interpreter) of the Quran is telling you this is غناء, Music, Musical instrument.", "Then you find the Hadith of the prophetﷺ, which is explicitly clear. By the way, there's a book by Sheikh alAlbani رحمه الله (May God have mercy on him); it's about تحريم آلات الطرب (Prohibition of Music instruments) or something close to that; if you Google it you'll find it. And he has many Ahadith that show you that musical instruments are Haram (prohibited). They talk about, for example: Drums and certain instruments, explicit Ahadith. But there's clear Hadith in Bukhari -the most authentic book of Hadith with the agreement of all the Muslims- that Hadith, what does it say? The Prophet says: لَيَكُونَنَّ مِنْ أُمَّتِي أَقْوَامٌ.. This is a funny thing: the people are fulfilling the prophecy of the Prophetﷺ. They are unknowingly fulfilling it. They're rejecting the Hadith, and they are fulfilling the prophecy! He says this Hadith is false, but they are fulfilling the prophecy of the Hadith. The Hadith is saying there will be a group of my people, they will do استحلال, meaning it's Haram and they will say it's Halal: Of خَمْرَ Alcohol, حِرَ Zina, حَرِيرَ Silk for men, because this is Haram, and مَعَازِفَ Musical instruments. And these people, they say to you: \"Do you know what, there is a disagreement, it is Halal. Disagreement is there\"! They say it or they don't say it? They say it! They fulfilled the prophecy of the Prophetﷺ.", "They rejected the Hadith: \"We don't accept this Hadith! It's مُعلّق!\" (Mu'allaq: One narrator or more is clearly missing at the beginning of the Chain of Narration). Even they never know in the Life what Mu'allaq is, and they never study the Science of Hadith, but today they become Scholars. They heard it somewhere: it's Mu'allaq! Mu'allaq means Bukhari put it but without a Chain. OK, Bukhari put it without a Chain; is there a chain for the Hadith or there's no Chain? \"We don't know, but it's Mu'allaq, therefore I'm not going to accept it.\" alHafidh Ibn Hajar al'Asqalani in his book تغليق التعليق, he put the chain for it. The same Hadith is in Musnad Ahmad and in multiple books with authentic narrations, authentic chains. When Bukhari mentioned it, Bukhari already knew its authenticity, he didn't necessarily need to mention it to you, and he narrated it from his teacher. There are certain Mua'llaaat that Bukhari mentioned بصيغة الجزم are authentic. But they don't know any of this, and they don't care to know. What they care to know is what? \"Some Sahabi said this and some Sahabi said that..\" Even though no one disagreed about this issue. You're not going to find a single companion who disagreed with Abdullah Ibn Abbas and Ibn Massoud when they talked about the interpretation of the verses that I told you. Open the Tafassir: you're not going to see them saying: \"No, this person is wrong, that's a wrong interpretation\". But they all become Scholars because of their desires. \"Music is OK, listen to music, stop being extremist.\" They listen to music. These are the diseases we have in this Ummah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ycNKKOx2jg", ((2728, "45:28–45:57"), (2763, "46:03–46:37"), (2802, "46:42–47:44"), (2871, "47:51–48:42"), (2932, "48:52–50:08"), (3008, "50:08–51:23"),))
