#passage(("Regarding how you can deal with things, what you can do, what you cannot do: there's a verse in the Quran where Allahﷻ says in the (Quran7:162-163). It's a command for us believers to say: قُلْ إِنَّ صَلَاتِى وَنُسُكِى وَمَحْيَاىَ وَمَمَاتِى لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ * لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُۥ ۖ وَبِذَٰلِكَ أُمِرْتُ وَأَنَا۠ أَوَّلُ ٱلْمُسْلِمِينَ (Say my prayer, the acts of worship that I do, my life and my death is only to Allahﷻ. He has no partners, and this is what I was commanded and I'm from the Muslims). This is the reason why we're in this life: we are in this life to obey Allahﷻ, we are in this life to follow the commands of Allahﷻ. There are clear prohibitions that Allahﷻ said do not do. Why did Allahﷻ say do not do these things? Because they are not good for you. If Allahﷻ said do not do them, then there is no good in them, no matter how much you love them. Allahﷻ says in the (Quran2:216): “وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تَكْرَهُواْ شَيْـًٔا وَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ۖ وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تُحِبُّواْ شَيْـًٔا وَهُوَ شَرٌّ لَّكُمْ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ” “You might love something and it's bad for you, you might hate something that is good for you, and Allah knows and you do not know”. So I can love something which is terrible, horrible, I can love something which is evil, bad for me, and I think it is good for me, but Allah knows best. And that is the point about submission: I'm a Muslim, I'm a submitter, I'm submitting to Allah, because I know Allah knows best, and when He says to me this it's not good, then that's not good.", "Of course, as you said, you can do these films without the music, without the Haram scenery; you can do. But you're not gonna be able to include these Haram things. I cannot give you a free pass and say: OK, I'm now going to play the legislator now, I'm gonna play on behalf of God now, I'm gonna tell you what you can and cannot do. No! No one can do that. If anyone does that, then they are now committing an act of disbelief, because they're trying to legislate with Allah. Allah already legislated what is right and wrong. Religion is perfect, it's complete 1400 years ago, what we can and what we cannot do.", "Now how many things are Halal, permissible, you can do? They are an infinite number. This is our nature as humans: we focus on the things which are not good, not allowed. This is our evil nature sometimes as humans. We try to focus on things that Allah says don't do. Allahﷻ, He's allowed you to do so many things; focus on those things which are Halal (permissible). And He's prohibited you from things because this life is a test, to prohibit you from engaging into these things.", "But take things step by step. Whatever you're going to do, it should not be a reason to stop you from accepting Islam, because there is no worse sin than not taking your Shahada, because if you die now you enter Hellfire. If you accept Islam and you do sins and you die, you're still punished, but you go to paradise in the end. So nothing should stop a person from taking that step, even if there is some issues that he might still struggle with.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Man Realises The Contradictions In Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CR6_RG9qdVM", ((765, "12:45–13:44"), (831, "13:51–14:12"), (858, "14:18–14:37"), (882, "14:42–14:56"),))
