#passage(("You find the statement, which is a completely clear statement, of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Al’as, where he said: مَنْ بَنَى بِبِلَادِ الْأَعَاجِمِ (Who's staying in the lands of the disbelievers) وَصَنَعَ نَيْرُوزَهُمْ وَمِهْرَجَانَهُمْ (Nayrouz and Mehrajan are just celebrations: he celebrated with them and gifted with them and did all of these things) وَتَشَبَّهَ بِهِمْ حَتَّى يَمُوتَ وَهُوَ كَذَلِكَ (and he dies in that state) حُشِرَ مَعَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ (he will be gathered with them on the Day of Judgment). This is a statement of a صحابي (Sahabi: a Companion of the Prophetﷺ), Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Al’as; this is not just your friend saying this. It's based on the Hadith of the Prophetﷺ من تشبَّهَ بقومٍ فَهوَ منْهم (Who imitates a group of people, he is from among them). Some people: \"oh you're being extreme\". I'm just telling you what the Prophetﷺ said. I'm reading to you what the Prophet is saying, what the Sahaba (Companions) are saying. It's not my opinion. The Prophetﷺ said من تشبَّهَ بقومٍ فَهوَ منْهم. And Shaikh Al Islam Ibn Taymiyya, he commented on that, and he said: The least thing you can take from this Hadith is whoever does that is committing a Major Sin, because if you take it as it's apparent, the person is committing Disbelief. He's a Disbeliever, because فَهوَ منْهم, he's from them! If you imitate Disbelievers you become? A Disbeliever! The least you could say is this is Haram. The least!", "And that's why the Prophetﷺ, when he went to Medina, he found out the people in Medina are celebrating different holidays that they had. So the Prophetﷺ he said: what is all of this? They said: the holidays. So the Prophetﷺ he said: أما نحن (but us) we have 2 holidays: Eid Al-Adha and Eid Al-Fitr. He didn't say: celebrate with them, gift with them, it's OK, it's a fun time, you can dance and have trees in the background. No! He said \"but us\". So what is this? A separation: \"but us\", which means there's us and them now. It's not a one group where everyone is doing the same mumbo jumbo; there's no such thing. \"But us\", meaning separation now: we have 2 holidays, we have Eid Al-Adha and Eid Al-Fitr. This is what we have as Muslims; these are the times in which you celebrate as a Muslim. Other than that, you don't go outside of this circle.", "And what is really the reason those people celebrate? What is the real problem in the Muslim Ummah? It's true, that's a part of it that we mentioned, which is the idea of compromise. But this is not the main issue. The main issue is imitating the Kuffar, imitating the Disbelievers. This is the core thing. The Prophetﷺ he said: لَتَتَّبِعُنَّ سَنَنَ مَن قَبْلَكُمْ: You will follow, you will tread the same steps that those who were before you tread, شبراً بشبر, like step by step; even if they enter into a hole, when the animals dig the hole and stay inside, you will go after them. And then the people asked: Jews and Christians? The Prophet said: who else! So the Prophetﷺ said that you will tread the same path, you will do the same thing that these people are doing.", "But then the Prophetﷺ, how was his life? If you read some of the books of Hadith, which unfortunately people are not doing, you have chapters. These chapters are titled what? باب مخالفة اليهود والنصارى (The Chapter of Going Against the Jews and the Christians). And in the chapter, tens of Ahadith of the Prophetﷺ: Trim your moustache and grow your beard, go against the Jews and the Christians. Pray in your shoes, because the Jews and Christians do not pray in their shoes. These are all Ahadith. Do not wear red clothes, just pure red, because this is the habit of the Jews and the Christians. Certain hairstyles: do not do this specific thing, because this is the habit of the Jews and the Christians.", "You see to which extent this was the case of the Prophetﷺ: even when the verse was revealed (Albaqarah2:222) وَیَسۡـَٔلُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلۡمَحِیضِۖ (They ask you about menstruation) قُلۡ هُوَ أَذࣰى فَٱعۡتَزِلُوا۟ ٱلنِّسَاۤءَ فِی ٱلۡمَحِیضِ (say it is harmful so stay away from intercourse with women within the period of menstruation), then they told the Prophetﷺ that the Jews at the time, they did not eat with their women, they did not touch their women, they stay away, different place from the women at the period of menstruation. So the Prophetﷺ he said: do everything except the intercourse. You can kiss your wife, you can hug your wife, you can eat with your wife, everything. Then when the Jews heard, they said: this man! -or Prophet Muhammadﷺ- he doesn't leave anything except he goes against us in! To that extent, this was a known thing; for them this is not one instance in which the Prophet said this. They said he's not leaving anything except that he is going against us in.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Reason Some \"Muslims\" Celebrate Christmas! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ti1oJEBzsOs", ((549, "9:09–10:29"), (635, "10:35–11:35"), (695, "11:35–13:12"), (798, "13:18–13:59"), (844, "14:04–14:57"),))
