#passage(("You don't have to go to a mosque. The prayer in the mosque is not an obligation for women. So unless a woman wants to go and pray in the mosque, she doesn't need to. The Prophet said: \"the prayer of a woman is better in her house than it is outside\". They can go to the mosque if they want. Absolutely, they're free to go to the mosque, if they want to pray in the mosque. But their prayer is even better in their homes, just more hidden between them and the Creator. That is even better, the Prophet said.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Baha'i Lady Questions Muslim On The Last Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5_h1_yrAXLg", ((1601, "26:41–27:28"),))
