#passage(("If you don't have water, it's two things: if you don't have access to water, or if water will harm you. For instance, there's a narration of prophet Muhammad and an individual that had a wound in his head, and he was covering his head, and he needed to do purification with water. So then he asked people: what should I do? They didn't know the ruling. And then they said to him: you have to use water. So he used the water and he died. Then the prophet got very angry, of course, because they killed the person. And then they said: \"Wasn't it enough for them, if they didn't know, that they would ask?\" And then he said: \"They killed him. May Allah kill them\", or something to that extent. He was very angry, of course, about what they did.", "So if the water is going to damage you, like some people: I just did an operation, I can't apply water here, for example, you wouldn't apply water on that part. You will have sand or dust or anything from that sense; you're going to do one hit, you're going to do this, and you're going to wipe your face. That's it, that's enough. But that's only for the exceptional situation in which water is not there or water is going to harm you. That is also mentioned in the Quran: Allah says \"if you do not find water\". It's not harmful; it's not bad for you to do this. It's not dirty. Just because it's called dirt doesn't mean it's going to hurt you. Sand: if I do this with sand, it's not bad for me. So, that's in the Quran, and it's in the hadith of how to do it, the method of doing it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Inquisitive Agnostic Grills Muslim On Cousin Marriage And Racism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fvVrT_WHQxg", ((2842, "47:22–48:08"), (2888, "48:08–49:00"),))
