#passage(("Do you mean the past tattoos or the future tattoos? That's the thing. So if someone had tattoos in his past, Islam doesn't talk about that. This something that you've done in your past before you become a Muslim, no one is going to tell you anything about that. If you want to remove them, that's up to you. If you don't want to remove them, keep them; there's no sin on you, that was before Islam.", "But after Islam, yes. The action of having tattoos is not accepted Islamically, is not allowed Islamically. It's one of the things which are considered a sin, as the Prophetﷺ said. It's actually considered a Major Sin as well, egregious sin. It's not something that is small, like here and there. It's something that is not allowed Islamically to do after someone becomes a Muslim. But if someone had it in his past, that is his past, and Allah forgives the past of anyone before he becomes a Muslim. A lot of people do things out of ignorance, out of not knowing what is right and wrong, out of being in their own communities. So Allah cannot hold someone accountable of something he did before he knew the truth. But when people know the truth and they become Muslim, now there are the teachings, and the guidance comes from Allah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Lady Learns The Truth About Palestine! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WKGqYmu6paw", ((1519, "25:19–25:33"), (1536, "25:36–26:13"),))
