#passage(("Smoking is Haram; not in my eyes, Islamically smoking is Haram. It's not about me, it's about what the text says. I'll tell you why it is Haram. But this is the thing: whichever a Muslim says to you something is Haram or Halal, they need to support that with evidence, because that Muslim is not someone who can legislate what is Halal and what is Haram. God is the only One Who legislates what is permissible and impermissible. In fact, if someone believes he can legislate with Allah, he's a Disbeliever; without a shadow of doubt, it takes you out of Islam. So if someone says to you this is OK or not OK, you ask him: where is your evidence that this is OK or not?", "Now why do I say to you smoking is Haram? Smoking is a new thing. It did not exist at the time of the Prophet, where they would be rolling tobacco and smoking. So how do we know that smoking is Haram? Does smoking cause you harm? Is there any doubt? The packet of cigarettes tells you: you're going to get cancer. The guy that is selling you is telling you: you're killing yourself. This is literally poison, but it's slow poison. It's like I'm giving you a bottle of poison and telling you: take 1ml each day and you're going to die after 30 years. Point is: you are killing yourself, you're harming your body, and that's explicitly Haram in the Quran(2:195). Allah says: \"Do not throw yourself into damnation.\" Do not kill yourselves. So that's the first thing, the aspect of the harm.", "And the Prophet said: do not harm yourself or anyone else. Now we're coming to anyone else. Smoking harms other people; does not only harm the environment, it harms me! When I get 70% of damage after your lung recycles the cigarettes, and then I inhale that recycle thing which comes up of your lung, what did I do to deserve that? So it also harms people around you.", "Now number 3 is also wasting money. If I take a 20£ note and I burn it, what's the difference between that and me smoking a cigarette? It's more healthy for me to burn the 20£ note instead of me smoking the cigarettes. So it's wasting money, and Allah commanded us not to waste money in the Quran, and He said those who waste money are the brothers of Satan, literally (Quran17:27). So wasting money is Haram, harming yourself and other people are Haram, and killing yourself is Haram; no one can come and say it's not Haram based on all of these evidences.", "It's relative to what you have. So let's assume I'm a millionaire. I buy a $10,000 watch, it's not wasting, because it's relative to the money that I have. So wasting is relative to what you have. So let's assume I have £2,000, I have 5 children, and I go gamble with £1,000, because I've got responsibilities and I need to take care of my children. So it's all relative to your situation; based on that, we can determine Islamically whether something is wasting or not. So wearing good clothes, for example, when you're someone who's got enough money, is not wasting, and it's not an act of arrogance as well. So it's something that is permissible, because the Prophet told us that Allah is Beautiful and He loves beauty. So us being beautiful, or trying to beautify ourselves in a permissible way, is a good thing. And Allah says in the Quran: قُلْ مَنْ حَرَّمَ زِينَةَ اللَّهِ (Quran7:32) (Who prohibited the adornment and the good things that Allah has given to the people). Who said don't take it? Allah's given it to you. So it's relative.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Visitor Questions Muslim On Hadith! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aVaXUL-Us6s", ((688, "11:28–12:04"), (729, "12:09–12:45"), (770, "12:50–13:05"), (790, "13:10–13:30"), (820, "13:40–14:35"),))
