#passage(("There is always certain things that people will have a struggle with, but if the Quran has a specific [ruling] on it, we take it. Prophet [ﷺ], he said: if someone hits, let him avoid the face. This is a whole Hadith that specifically here is telling you the prohibition of hitting in the face directly, and the scholars explain: because the face of a human being is honored, and it's unlike the rest of the body; it's the most honorable part of that individual, of that human, of the person. In fighting war against armies, someone trying to fight, this is a different context. Scholars would say this is an exception, which you can do this.", "But for fun, people would use the term UFC, or boxing, or it's not just UFC, it's just like any sport, or you and your friends sitting in the restaurant, whatever it is, later on you go and you want to hit each other: that prohibition is there, is that you cannot hit the face. I'm sure that you could learn [self-defense], you could learn many beneficial things without the necessity of hitting an individual directly in the face. Because a lot of people say \"oh, but this is the intention of strengthening yourself\". But that's not a necessity, because you can strengthen yourself in a way in which you don't need to do that. So do not use it as an excuse when it's not a necessity. If it's a necessity, it's a different story. Holding the sword, holding a piece of metal when you trying to learn: these are necessities. They were fighting with swords, so there's no alternative. So when it comes to necessity, different situation, but for self-defense you can learn many other means of self-defense without needing to hit someone in the face. Allah knows best.", "You have narrations to do with companions, for example, engaging in wrestling, and certain [martial] arts or sports can be beneficial and strengthen someone's body. But I think what you're referring to is more for fun, for entertainment. So if you're saying that that would be linked to UFC, bringing two people in the cage, instead of bringing two balls hitting each other in the head, they bring two human beings hitting each other in the face, and to make money, for the people's entertainment: from that aspect I get what you're saying. You can have gambling, you can have entertainment, you can have promotion of drugs and alcohol; all of these things come with this problem. And Allah knows best.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((3663, "1:01:03–1:01:59"), (3719, "1:01:59–1:03:18"), (3838, "1:03:58–1:04:44"),))
